{
 "encounter_id": "00821",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "NURSE",
  "person_4": "CLINICAL_STAFF"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "Mrs Tully? I'm Orla on reception. The doctor's running ten minutes late, but the nurse can take your measurements. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh, that's fine, I'm in no rush. I'm a bit vague today, I haven't slept. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'm Rhona, the nurse. Blood pressure 130 over 80, pulse 76, oxygen 98 percent.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Hello, Mrs Tully. This is your health check, isn't it? Anything on your mind? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Well, nothing really. Only I get a burning in my upper tummy, after meals. I didn't think it was worth mentioning."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Tell me about it. How often?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A few times a week. A hot, burning feeling, under my ribs. It's worse after a big meal, or tomato sauce."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any vomiting, or trouble swallowing?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any black stools, or weight loss? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, I've actually put weight on. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What are you taking at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A blood pressure tablet, ramipril, 5 mg once a day. And a vitamin D tablet, 800 units, every morning."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any conditions apart from the blood pressure?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "High blood pressure, and I've had an underactive thyroid since the nineties."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My gallbladder, taken out in 2008."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any family history of stomach problems or bowel cancer?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My mother had a stomach ulcer, and my brother had bowel polyps."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And do you smoke, or drink alcohol?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I don't smoke. A glass of wine, most evenings."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, would you like me to do her breathing check?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please, Rhona, thanks. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Mrs Tully, any breathlessness or wheeze?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing at all."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Any chest pain with the burning?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. It's right under the ribs, not in my chest."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me press your tummy.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh, careful, that's tender. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A little tender at the top, in the middle, and nothing else."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that normal? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fairly. Burning after meals is very common, and I'm not going to put a name on it today. But because of your age and your family history, I'd like to check a few things. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What sort of things? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to arrange a breath test for the stomach bacterium, Helicobacter pylori."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll give you the instructions about stopping tablets, Mrs Tully. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Meanwhile, eat smaller meals, avoid tomato, spicy food, and coffee late in the day, and leave three hours between your last meal and bed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I like my wine with dinner. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It may be adding to it, so try to cut back a little."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll try. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks. If you vomit, find it hard to swallow, or notice black stools, come back sooner."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Thank you, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
